cPanel's own scores are 5.3 under CVSS 4.0 for CVE-2026-29202 and CVE-2026-29203 ([EUVD-2026-28811](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-28811); [EUVD-2026-28812](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-28812)) and 8.6 under CVSS 3.1 for CVE-2026-29201 ([EUVD-2026-28810](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-28810)); the 8.8, 8.8 and 4.3 figures are The Hacker News's ([The Hacker News, 2026-05-09](https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/cpanel-whm-patch-3-new-vulnerabilities.html)). Only CVE-2026-29202 yields code execution: CVE-2026-29203 lets a user chmod an arbitrary file ([cPanel, CVE-2026-29203](https://support.cpanel.net/hc/en-us/articles/40311543760407-Security-CVE-2026-29203-cPanel-WHM-WP2-Security-Update-May-08-2026)) and CVE-2026-29201 makes an arbitrary file world-readable ([cPanel, CVE-2026-29201](https://support.cpanel.net/hc/en-us/articles/40311033698327-Security-CVE-2026-29201-cPanel-WHM-WP2-Security-Update-May-08-2026)). The patch and the advisories were published together on 2026-05-08, and the fix covers eleven cPanel & WHM branches from 11.86 to 11.136 and WP Squared, not three ([cPanel, CVE-2026-29202](https://support.cpanel.net/hc/en-us/articles/40311426610327-Security-CVE-2026-29202-cPanel-WHM-WP2-Security-Update-May-08-2026)). For CVE-2026-41940, Shadowserver counted at least 44,000 likely compromised IP addresses scanning its honeypots on 2026-04-30 ([The Hacker News, 2026-05-04](https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/critical-cpanel-vulnerability.html)), and KnownHost reported exploitation since 2026-02-23 ([SecurityWeek, 2026-04-30](https://www.securityweek.com/critical-cpanel-whm-vulnerability-exploited-as-zero-day-for-months/)); no source describes attackers chaining it with CVE-2026-29202.
